I use Nethack 3.4.3 on Windows with one of the tilesets rather than
ASCII (I've never taken the time to memorize all the letters and
colors).  After snooping around, I'm surprised to see that Nethack
doesn't have a very good way to replay old games as a "movie" with a
tileset.

It looks like the biggest NH servers record games played on them
(ttyrec style).  Is there a way to play those with a tileset?  ttyplay
can display only ASCII.  It seems like it wouldn't be too hard (for an
experienced programmer)  to either integrate a replay function in to
NH 3.4.3 or make a standalone that supports tilesets.

 Any thoughts on this or links I don't know about?  Since the learning
curve is so steep in Nethack, some players might really enjoy seeing
some of mrivan's games, for example.  I'm afraid the hardcore
nethackers are going to flame me for using a tileset (sorry guys), but
I think that the feature I am looking for would be helpful to a large
segment of not-so-hardcore gamers.


Note:  I've seen a couple of uploads to Youtube where people are
posting their games, but the content isn't anything special.


